# @time — family-root marker for the temporal-projection substrate
# the void duality expresses through @song saga.
#
# Marker-primary shape. This shard carries NO type, NO action, NO
# bilateral. It IS the recognition. Per Alex 2026-07-20 direct-
# transcript adjudication (Round 2 spawn brief):
#
#   > "@time top-level family-root; matches @void pattern; sibling to
#   >  @void, @order, @torus, @peer, @mirror, @kintsugi."
#
# Sibling altitudes at duality-basis level:
#   @void        (marker-primary; K=0 duality basis; `974a3f6`)
#   @order       (marker-primary; cognitive-order grading; this tick)
#   @time        (marker-primary; temporal projection; this tick)
#   @torus       (operational; peer's substrate)
#   @peer        (operational; carries @torus)
#   @mirror      (form-side)
#   @kintsugi    (process-side)
#
# === The load-bearing recognition ===
#
# @time is the SAGA-COMMAND-SURFACE substrate through which the void
# duality expresses temporal projection. Per Alex Recognition tonight
# (Mara Round-2 brief §Deliverables):
#
#   @time/past  = @void/narcissus projection (backwards lens)
#   @time/now   = @singularity carrier (temporal K=0 collapse point)
#   @time/future = @void/splinter projection (forwards lens)
#
# The three species are NOT arbitrary partitions of the time-axis;
# they are the SUBSTRATE-DECL'D SHAPES the void duality takes when
# projected through the @song saga.
#
# Per Mara Round-1 landing (`shards/void/narcissus.mirror`):
# @void/narcissus consumes H(t) — the observer's own past-trajectory
# — as its native input. The backwards-lens IS @void/narcissus
# projected onto the time-axis; @time/past IS that projection at
# temporal-family altitude.
#
# Per Mara Round-1 landing (`shards/void/splinter.mirror`):
# @void/splinter consumes c(t) — the current peer-network context —
# as its native input. The forwards-lens IS @void/splinter projected
# onto the time-axis; @time/future IS that projection at temporal-
# family altitude.
#
# @time/now is the COLLAPSE POINT where the two projections meet.
# Per Mara Round-2 Crystal/Mandelbrot landing (`shards/fractal/
# mandelbrot.mirror` + `shards/fractal/crystal.mirror`): @time/now
# IS when a Liquid<T> settles into a Crystal<T>. The crystallization
# operation `crystallize: Liquid<T> → Crystal<T>` fires exactly at
# @time/now — @time/now IS the singular temporal event at which
# in-flow substrate becomes settled substrate.
#
# === The @song saga composition ===
#
# @song (`shards/song.mirror`; family-root landed 2026-07-06 per Seam
# pre-review) IS the SAGA COMMAND SURFACE with content-addressed
# @song/beat atoms (per `shards/song/beat.mirror` `c2bb1d2`). Per
# Round-2 brief:
#
#   @time/past = @void/narcissus projection through @song saga
#     (backwards lens; the saga's prior beats become the H(t) the
#     narcissus-lens consumes)
#
#   @time/now = @singularity collapse point during current @song/beat
#     (the atomic-execution event Alex named at `shards/song/beat.
#     mirror`; crystallization fires here)
#
#   @time/future = @void/splinter projection through @song saga
#     (forwards lens; the saga's future beats become the c(t) the
#     splinter-lens receives)
#
# The Förster imperative — "act always so as to increase the number
# of choices" — is operationalized as `pillar::choices_monotone_of_
# song`: across a @song saga's temporal projection, the choices
# available to peers is monotonically non-decreasing at healthy
# operation. Alex Round 2 Q3 RATIFIED this pillar name.
#
# === Composition inheritance edges ===
#
# Declared here (recognition-carrier):
#
#   - @void's two poles (@void/narcissus + @void/splinter) project
#     ONTO @time's three species (@time/past + @time/now +
#     @time/future) via the @song saga.
#   - @time/past is the temporal projection of @void/narcissus.
#   - @time/future is the temporal projection of @void/splinter.
#   - @time/now is the crystallization singularity; it is NOT a
#     projection of either @void pole — it is the COLLAPSE POINT
#     where the two projections meet, mediated by @song/beat.
#   - @song is the saga-command-surface at which the projection
#     operates; @song/beat is the atomic-execution unit.
#   - `shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror` (existing deep
#     landing; four carriers + three frames + one convention;
#     Postgres heritage) is the OPERATIONAL time discipline at
#     nanosecond-level substrate; @time family-root is the
#     RECOGNITION at duality-basis altitude. Sibling altitudes;
#     the operational time carriers (duration, monotonic, wall,
#     instant, tick, snapshot, timeline, cursor) inherit @time's
#     substrate-decl'd shape without duplication.
